# Normalize line endings in the repository to LF.
#
# This repo had mixed endings: some files stored CRLF, some LF. That makes a
# whole-file rewrite indistinguishable from a real edit — a 5-line change to
# src/server.ts showed up as 2,573 changed lines, which hides the actual change
# from review. Any tool that reads and rewrites a file (an editor with a
# different default, a script, a formatter) silently flips the whole file.
#
# text=auto eol=lf stores LF in Git and checks out LF everywhere. This service
# runs in a Linux container, so LF is also what it executes with.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-native scripts must keep CRLF to remain runnable on Windows.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Never touch binaries — normalization would corrupt them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary
